# Cloudflare Pages response headers: the Pages counterpart of docker/nginx.conf.
# Copied into the build output by `npm run build:pages` (pages/finish-build.mjs).
# Syntax: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# Every matching rule applies, in file order, and a header set twice is joined with commas, so a
# later rule detaches Cache-Control ("! Cache-Control") before setting its own.

# Everything is revalidated on each load (the SPA shell: / and every client-side route Pages
# answers with index.html), so a deploy is picked up at once.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Deployment-specific: never let a browser keep a stale copy.
/config.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-store

# No long cache for the fingerprinted bundles (main-*, chunk-*, media/*): Pages answers a request
# for a file that does not exist with index.html (SPA fallback, 200), so an "immutable" rule would
# pin that HTML in the browser for a stale chunk name, and a rollback to that build would then break
# for that browser. Revalidating (no-cache above; Pages sends ETags, so unchanged files are 304s)
# keeps them correct.
